# ORANGE test and clean restore gate

Read `docs/archive/ORANGE_TEST_AND_CLEAN_RESTORE_POLICY.md` and the current round record before test writes, backup/restore or performance work. Follow ORANGE_AGENT_READ_FIRST.txt as well. The policy was approved by the owner on 2026-11-21; use later explicit owner decisions if changed and archive them.

Never infer a ready baseline from a filename, nonempty ZIP, old chat, or empty products table. Record baseline identity/status, schema+commit, retention protection, writer, test effects and last safe action. If readiness or round state is unknown, continue independent reading/preparation but do not create test business data. Destructive restore/delete requires owner approval for the concrete snapshot and scope at execution time. Preserve real and enduring data, test evidence, and cross-session history.

Never open `.env.php`, extract passwords, or download hosting backups. Backups remain private on the hosting. DB+uploads does not cover all runtime flags, caches or sessions; verify these after cleanup without indiscriminate deletion.

Track OR-PERF-016 with before/after measurements. A browser timeout is not proof of server cause. Do not remove schema guards, validation, country isolation or authorization to improve speed. Keep minimal diffs and the existing Git deployment workflow.

Current round state is external and must be read fresh from https://chatgpt.com/space/page_50fb21e7e8388191a414234def513012 or a current owner-provided verified handoff. This rule does not create a backup or start a test. Refresh these committed instructions in the existing local workspace while preserving uncommitted work; never force-reset it.
